abstract: "PerceptionTests is a Windows desktop application written in C#/WPF for psychoacoustic research in Auditory Scene Analysis. It supports behavioural estimation of auditory stream-segregation thresholds through deterministic synthesis of pure-tone stimuli as 44.1 kHz mono PCM waveforms. The software integrates JSON-defined experimental sessions, configurable tone-duration scheduling, stimulus-aligned response logging, checkpoint persistence, dynamic questionnaire rendering, and structured participant-data capture. Experiment and questionnaire configurations are researcher-editable and validated at startup. Results, questionnaire data, configuration snapshots, and metadata are exported as machine-readable JSON files. By combining explicit waveform synthesis, documented configuration, structured export, and automated tests, PerceptionTests supports reproducible studies of auditory stream formation across participant groups."
keywords:
  - auditory scene analysis
  - psychoacoustics
  - stream-segregation threshold
  - csharp
  - wpf
  - pcm synthesis
